hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3594","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"They say that the Messenger of Allah made a will concerning 'Ali"
"3595","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah died when no one was with him except me.\"\" She said: \"\"And he called for a vessel"
"3596","It was narrated from 'Amir bin Sa'd that his father said:\"\"I became ill with a sickness from which I later recovered. The Messenger of Allah came to visit me"
"3597","It was narrated that Sa'd said:\"\"The Prophet came to visit me when I was in Makkah. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"3598","It was narrated from 'Amir bin Sa'd that his father said:\"\"The Prophet used to visit him when he was in Makkah"
"3599","One from the family of Sa'd narrated:\"\"Sa'd fell sick and the Messenger of Allah entered upon him and he said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"3600","Amir bin Sa'd (narrated) from his father that he fell sick in Makkah and the Messenger of Allah came to him. When Sa'd saw him"
"3601","It was narrated that Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah visited me when I was sick"
"3602","It was narrated from Sa'd that the Prophet visited him when he was sick"
"3603","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah came to visit Sa'd (when he was sick). Sa'd said to him:\"\"O Messenger of Allah"
"3604","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\"\"If the people were to reduce (their bequests) to one-quarter (of their wealth"
"3605","It was narrated that 'Umar said:\"I asked the Messenger of Allah about some land of mine in Thamgh. He said: 'Freeze it and donate its fruits.'\""
"3606",""
"3607","It was narrated from Jabir that his father died owing debts. \"\"I came to the Prophet and said:'(O Messenger of Allah!) My father has died owing debts"
"3608",""
"3609","It was narrated that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\"\"My father owed some dates to a Jew. He was killed on the Day of Uhud and he left behind two gardens. The dates owed to the Jew would take up everything in the two gardens. The Prophet said: 'Can you take half this year and half next year?' But the Jew refused. The Prophet said: 'When the time to pick the dates comes"
"3610","It was narrated that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\"\"My father died owing debts. I offered to his creditors that they could take the fruits in lieu of what he owed them"
